$ ##########################################################################











$ The following assessments are incorporated in this database:



$



$ ... see list of publications in the reference section



$ at the end of this file ...











$ The following elements are included in this database:



$



$ Fe, Al, B, C, Co, Cr, Cu, H, Hf, La, Mn, Mo, N, Nb, Ni, O, P, Pd, S, Si,



$ Ti, V, W, Y







$ This database has been optimised inside the following limits:



$ Temperature: 673 K - 2000 K



$



$ Alloy composition (wt.%): Al<3  B<0.5  C<0.5  Co<3  Cr<25  Cu<1  Hf<0.5



$ La<0.5  MN<25  Mo<5  N<1  Nb<1  Ni<26  O<0.5  P<0.005  Pd<4  S<0.5  Si<3.5



$ Ti<0.5  V<0.5  W<3  Y<0.5







$ H: Only binary Fe-H parameters in fcc and bcc are edited.;







$ Typical applications: 9-12% Cr steels, hot-work tool steels,



$ microalloyed steels, austenitic stainless steels, PH maraging steels.







$ The following phases are included in this database:



$ They are listed in the order of their appearance in



$ part D) Thermodynamic model parameters for phases.;



$ For their documentation see part D).



$ Documentation and priority rankings suggested by the editor are visible



$ in the MatCalc databases window after reading the database



$ and marking the phase of interest.



$



$ LIQUID



$



$ FCC_A1



$ BCC_A2



$ HCP_A3



$



$ ALPHA_MN



$ BETA_MN



$ BETA_RHOMBO_B



$ DIAMOND_A4



$ GRAPHITE



$



$ Ordered phases (split model used)



$ BCC_B2



$



$ Intermetallic phases



$ CHI_A12  CO3 MO  CO3 V  COV3  CR3 MN5  G_PHASE  LAVES_PHASE  MNNI



$ MNNI2  MNNI_T3  MU_PHASE  MU_PHASE_I  ETA NITI2  R_PHASE  SIGMA  FE17 Y2



$ NI5 Y  PDFE_L12  PDMN_AF  PDMN_P  PDMN_B2  PD2 MN  PD3 MN  Pd5 MN3  PD6 FE5 MN2



$



$ Carbides



$ CEMENTITE  CR2 VC2  K_CARB  KSI_CARBIDE  M3 C2  M6 C



$ M7 C3  M12 C  M23 C6  MOC_ETA  V3 C2  WC



$



$ Metastable transition carbides



$ EPS_CARB  ETA_CARB  FE24 C10  KSI_FE5 C2



$



$ Nitrides



$ ALN  ALN_EQU  BN_HP4  CR3 NI2 SIN FE4 N  MN6 N4  MN6 N5  MNSIN2  SI3 N4  ZET



$



$ Borides



$ CRB  CR2 B  CR5 B3  FEB  FENBB  FE3 NB3 B4  M2 B  MNB2  MNB4  O_MN2 B  MN3 B4



$ MOB  MOB2  MO2 M1 B2  NBB  NB3 B2  M5 B6  TIB  TIB2  TI3 B4



$



$ Sulfides



$ A_CHALC  ANILITE  B_CHALC  COVELLITE  CU2 S  DIGENITE



$ DISULF  DJURLEITE  FC_MONO  FC_ORTHO  FES_P  MNS_Q  PYRR  TIS



$



$ Carbo-sulfides



$ TI4 C2 S2



$



$ Oxides



$ Simple oxide models without considering of



$ cation and oxygen nonstoichiometries are used.



$ CORUND  HALITE  HF1 O2_M  HF1 O2_T  HF1 O2_C  LA2 O3_A  LA2 O3_H  LA2 O3_C  SIO2



$ SPINEL  TI2 O3  TIO2  TRID  Y2 O3_H  Y2 O3_C  YALO3  Y4 AL2 O9  Y2 TIO5  Y2 TI2 O7



$



$ Phosphides



$ M2 P  M3 P



$



$ Special phases



$ BCC_DISL



